+/*
+===============================================================================
+
+	visionOS stereo 3D — the offscreen present PAIRS (openQ4-ios D-100, D-101).
+
+	In 3D the engine renders the COMPLETE composite (scene + HUD + menus +
+	console) into offscreen images instead of the window swapchain, and the
+	shell's CompositorServices thread draws them onto a world-locked panel.
+	Nothing is imported into Vulkan: under MoltenVK the VkImage IS a MTLTexture,
+	so the hand-off is vkGetMTLTextureMVK and a Metal blit on the compositor's
+	own queue.
+
+	The swapchain is BYPASSED, not torn down: the window's surface and its
+	swapchain stay alive and untouched, so leaving 3D needs no recreate.
+
+	ROUND 3 CHANGES TWO THINGS ABOUT ROUND 2's MONO PATH:
+
+	1. A present buffer is a PAIR of images, left and right, and it is published
+	   ATOMICALLY. The engine renders both eyes per host frame at the same game
+	   time (idSessionLocal::UpdateScreen), so a pair is the unit the compositor
+	   must see: showing a left eye from frame N beside a right eye from frame
+	   N-1 is vertical-disparity nausea, not a cheap frame. Nothing is published
+	   until BOTH eyes' fences have been observed signalled.
+
+	2. The eye extent is DECOUPLED from the window. The present images, their
+	   depth images, vkExec.activeExtent and glConfig.vidWidth/Height all follow
+	   r_stereo3dWidth/Height while 3D is on; the swapchain keeps its own size
+	   and the window is free to be parked to a small card without touching the
+	   panel's resolution. D-097 made this mandatory rather than nice: two eyes
+	   at the window's 2560x1440 cost ~10.6 ms, over every rate budget there is.
+
+	SEVERAL pairs, for the reason the swapchain has more than one image: a frame
+	still in flight must never be the one the compositor is reading, and the
+	pair the compositor is reading must never be the one the next frame
+	overwrites. How many, and the fence rule that publishes them, are the
+	subject of the block below.
+
+===============================================================================
